{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>For he was a son of old age to him.</b> He was born to him at the time of his old age. And Onkelos (Onkelos on Genesis 37:3) translated \"אֲרֵי בַר חַכִּים הוּא לֵהּ\" (for he was a wise son to him), because everything he had learned from Shem and Eber he handed down to him. Another matter: his facial countenance resembled his, the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 37:3). And Rabbi Abraham (Ibn Ezra on Genesis 37:3) similarly said: כִּי בֶן זְקֻנִים — that he begot him in his old age, and he was ninety-one years old, and also his brother Benjamin they called a young child of old age. But this is not correct in my eyes, for Scripture says that he loved Joseph more than all his brothers because he was a בֶּן זְקֻנִים, yet all his sons were born to him in his old age, and behold Issachar and Zebulun are no more than a year or two older than Joseph. And what seems right in my eyes is that it was the custom of elders to take one of their younger sons to be with him to attend him, and he would lean on his hand constantly and never part from him, and he was called his בֶּן זְקֻנִים because he attended him in his old age. Now Jacob took Joseph for this purpose, and he was with him constantly, and therefore he would not go with the flock when they pastured in a distant place. And Onkelos, who said \"בַּר חַכִּים,\" intends to say that he was a discerning and wise son in his father's eyes, and his reason follows the sense of זְקֵנִים, and in the phrase יֶלֶד זְקוּנִים he translated \"בַּר סֵבְתִין,\" because Scripture did not say here כִּי בֶן זְקֻנִים הָיָה but rather said הוּא לוֹ — that he was such in his eyes. And this is their intention when they say (Genesis Rabbah 84:8): everything he learned from Shem and Eber he handed down to him — to say that he handed down to him wisdoms and secrets of Torah, and he found him discerning and a master of their hidden meaning, as though he were an elder and advanced in years:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:40:58.990585625Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}